  "goodToKnow": "Der Heiland is the Saviour, a traditional name for Jesus Christ in hymns and prayers: Der Heiland ist geboren. A synonym is der Erlöser (redeemer). It comes from an old present participle of heilen (to heal, save). Figuratively and often ironically, someone hailed as a Heiland is treated as a saviour. The Old Saxon epic Heliand (9th century) retells the Gospels. It has no plural."
